    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "A Man of His Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The banality of evil is brilliantly exposed in this thought-provoking and singular portrait of a mediocre yet ambitious bureaucrat in Nazi-occupied France."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/coward-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Coward"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Lukas Dhont’s latest gem is a luminous and deeply romantic love story, set against the backdrop of the First World War."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/woman-unknown-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Woman Unknown"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In May el-Toukhy’s powerful third feature, Marie, a survivor with secrets, navigates retribution and the febrile chaos of life in post-war Denmark."
    }
